2. Project Development Phases
Phase 1: Requirement Analysis
Objective
The first phase focuses on understanding the educational problems faced by students and identifying the requirements of the proposed system.
Activities
•	Identify the target users.
•	Analyze common student learning difficulties.
•	Identify the limitations of traditional learning support.
•	Define the functionality required from the AI assistant.
•	Determine hardware and software requirements.
•	Identify the AI technology to be integrated.
•	Define functional and non-functional requirements.
Functional Requirements
The system should allow users to:
1.	Enter academic questions.
2.	Receive AI-generated answers.
3.	Ask follow-up questions.
4.	Request simplified explanations.
5.	Generate summaries.
6.	Generate quizzes and practice questions.
7.	Interact with the assistant through a conversational interface.
Non-Functional Requirements
•	User-friendly interface
•	Fast response time
•	Reliability
•	Scalability
•	Security
•	Maintainability
•	Availability
Deliverable
Software Requirement Specification (SRS) containing the complete requirements of EduGenie.
